Most supply chain risk reviews start from supplier questionnaires. They describe the network as procurement believes it to be, not as goods actually move through it.

## Instrument the Real Network

Lead-time variance, port dwell times and inventory turns tell a more honest story. Mapping them across tiers usually reveals two or three chokepoints that carry a disproportionate share of risk.

## Automate the Containment

Once chokepoints are known, pre-approved playbooks — alternate routing, buffer releases, supplier switching — can trigger automatically when thresholds are crossed, cutting response time from weeks to hours.
